{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" let a game split its ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"own"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" world across types and packages. A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"plugin"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" goes one step further: it packages a reusable game ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"system"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — commerce, combat, dialog, magic — as an importable unit of verbs and rules that any game can opt into. Instead of hand-copying the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"buy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"sell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" logic into every shop game, you write it once as a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and splice it in.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A plugin is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"logic only","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". It contributes the player-typeable vocabulary a system needs and the rules that react to it, but it owns no rooms, items, or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"text":" state of its own. It operates over entities and state the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"host"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" game declares, receiving what it needs as parameters. That’s what keeps it portable — it assumes nothing about the host’s world beyond the traits and intents they agree on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-plugin-is-a-GamePlugin","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"A plugin is a `GamePlugin`"},{"code":["extension Intent {","    #verb(\"haggle\", [\"haggle\", \"over\", .directObject])","}","","struct CommercePlugin: GamePlugin {","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] {","        .haggle","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"actions","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" all default to empty, so a plugin declares only what it needs. The "},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declarations (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") give the plugin "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" its hosts the same typed constants — host rules key on "},{"code":".haggle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" exactly as the plugin’s verbs emit it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note what "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"isn’t"}]},{"type":"text","text":" declared here. "},{"code":"buy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"sell","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are engine stub verbs (see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StubVerbs"},{"type":"text","text":"), so the words are already in every game’s vocabulary; a commerce plugin only has to supply the behavior, which it does with the rules below. "},{"code":"haggle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is genuinely the plugin’s own, so it needs the "},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"code":"GnustoMeleeCombat","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" splits the same way: the "},{"code":"attack","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" family is promoted, "},{"code":"stab","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"strike"},{"type":"text","text":" are added."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" splice the same way (","type":"text"},{"code":"var timers: [TimedEvent] { actors.timers }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and parameterized timer ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"factories","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — methods returning a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent","type":"reference"},{"text":" for the host’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block — are how a plugin animates the host’s actors on the end-of-turn clock. Timer names are global to the game: prefix yours by convention (","type":"text"},{"code":"\"actors.roam\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-host-splices-verbs-and-rules","text":"The host splices verbs and rules"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host stores the plugin as a plain property and splices its vocabulary into its own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbs"},{"type":"text","text":" block. A plain plugin property is neither a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", nor "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":", so the bootstrap’s reflection walk ignores it — it never becomes an entity and never collides."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".price","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" below is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"TraitKey<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" declared once (","type":"text"},{"code":"extension TraitKey<Int> { static let price = Self(\"price\") }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") — see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct LampShop: Game {","    let commerce = CommercePlugin()","    @Global var purse = Purse(coins: 10)          \/\/ the HOST owns the wallet","    let lantern = Item { name(\"brass lantern\"); trait(.price, 5) }","","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { commerce.verbs }    \/\/ splice the vocabulary","    \/\/ rules below","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Parameterized-rules-over-host-entities","text":"Parameterized rules over host entities","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin’s rules need the host’s own lantern and purse — things it can’t know about in advance. So rules that touch host state are exposed as "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"parameterized methods"}]},{"type":"text","text":" returning "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules"},{"type":"text","text":", which the host calls with its own declarations. The wallet is handed in as closures that read and adjust the host’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":"; they run under the live turn, so they see and mutate state exactly as an inline rule would."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension CommercePlugin {","    @RuleBuilder","    func purchase(","        of item: Item,","        balance: @escaping @Sendable () -> Int,","        charge:  @escaping @Sendable (Int) -> Void","    ) -> Rules {","        item.before(.buy) {","            let price = item[.price] ?? 0","            guard balance() >= price else {","                try refuse(\"You can't afford the \\(item.name); it costs \\(price) coins.\")","            }","            charge(price)","            try reply(\"You buy the \\(item.name) for \\(price) coins. You have \\(balance()) left.\")","        }","    }","}","","\/\/ in the host:","var rules: Rules {","    commerce.purchase(of: lantern,","                      balance: { purse.coins },","                      charge:  { purse.coins -= $0 })","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The protocol’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":" requirement is for self-contained, world-scoped rules that need nothing from the host; anything host-specific goes through a factory method like this."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"A-plugin-can-contribute-only-vocabulary","text":"A plugin can contribute only vocabulary","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The rules are optional. A plugin can teach the parser a word and leave the behavior to the host, which handles the shared intent in its own ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension Intent {","    #verb(\"appraise\", [\"appraise\", .directObject])","}","","struct Appraiser: GamePlugin {","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] {","        .appraise","    }","}","","\/\/ in the host:","var rules: Rules {","    gem.before(.appraise) {","        try reply(\"The \\(gem.name) is worth \\(gem[.price] ?? 0) coins.\")","    }","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-one-thing-the-host-doesnt-splice","text":"The one thing the host doesn’t splice","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin\/statusFields"},{"type":"text","text":" adds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name=value"},{"type":"text","text":" pairs to the play-test status footer, and it is the single member the host gets by "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"storing"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the plugin rather than by splicing it into a block of its own:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Barometer: GamePlugin {","    var statusFields: [(String, String)] { [(\"glass\", \"falling\")] }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything else here changes what the game does, so the host opts in by hand. A status field annotates a transcript the host already asked for and changes nothing about the world — and there is no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Game","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block to splice it into — so the bootstrap reads it off the host’s stored properties, the same walk that catches an unlisted bundle. A plugin the host stores is found; one constructed inline inside a computed property is not.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The field is read inside a live turn frame that is then discarded, so it must be read-only — and it is sampled at the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"close","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" of the turn rather than after the turn’s counter advanced, so a field derived from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"moves"},{"type":"text","text":" names the turn it is printed under. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles#A-bundle-can-add-a-field-to-the-status-footer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the full contract, sampling point included, which is identical for both protocols."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Content-bearing plugins own their region","type":"heading","anchor":"Content-bearing-plugins-own-their-region","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A logic-only "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" declares no world of its own — it operates entirely over entities the host passes it. A plugin that needs to ship its "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"own"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" rooms, items, and "},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" state is a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles"},{"type":"text","text":" instead: a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent"},{"type":"text","text":" carries "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the bootstrap discovers its entities by reflection, "},{"isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"namespacing","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"namespacing","type":"text"}],"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles#EntityIDs-are-namespaced-by-the-bundle"},{"type":"text","text":" them under the bundle so a reusable plugin can’t collide with the host. List it in the game’s "},{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The two roles compose in one type. A single struct can conform to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent"},{"text":" (for its auto-namespaced region and self-contained rules) ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}]},{"text":" expose host-facing rule factories exactly like a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin"},{"text":" — factories are just methods returning ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules"},{"text":", so any type can offer them:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension Intent {","    #verb(\"donate\", [\"donate\", .directObject])","}","","struct ShrineContent: GameContent {","    let shrine = Location { name(\"Stone Shrine\"); description(\"…\") }   \/\/ its own room","    @Global var visits = 0                                             \/\/ its own state","","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { .donate }","    var rules: Rules { shrine.onEnter { visits += 1; try reply(\"…\") } }  \/\/ self-contained","","    \/\/ Host-facing factory over a host item + host global — the GamePlugin pattern.","    func offering(of item: Item,","                  merit: @escaping @Sendable () -> Int,","                  credit: @escaping @Sendable (Int) -> Void) -> Rules {","        item.before(.donate) { credit(item[.value] ?? 0)","            try reply(\"Your merit rises to \\(merit()).\") }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host lists it in "},{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (registering the namespaced region) "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" splices the factory into its own "},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", wiring it to host declarations:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct PilgrimGame: Game {","    let shrineKit = ShrineContent()","    @Global var merit = 0","    let coin = Item { name(\"brass coin\"); trait(.value, 7) }","","    var content: GameContents { shrineKit }","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { shrineKit.verbs }","    var rules: Rules {","        shrineKit.offering(of: coin, merit: { merit }, credit: { merit += $0 })","    }","    \/\/ map: place coin in shrineKit.shrine, wire plaza ↔ shrineKit.shrine, …","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"References stay token-based across the boundary, so a host item can sit in a plugin room and a plugin rule can hook a host entity regardless of the namespace."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The first-party plugins","anchor":"The-first-party-plugins","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Seven shipped library products exercise both plugin shapes for real — each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"imports only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gnusto"},{"type":"text","text":", and the Zork 1 executable target is the worked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example that wires the first four:"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shape"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Owns"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The host passes","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoDangerousDark"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one dark-turn counter, the grue daemon","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"prose + grace period at init; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"suspended"},{"text":" to make the dark harmless for a stretch (never ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stopDaemon(\"grue\")"},{"text":", which freezes the count)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoScoring","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"award-once registers"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the award table to "},{"code":"init(awards:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", treasures + the trophy case to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"treasures(_:into:)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoActors","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GamePlugin"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"nothing — position ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"is"}]},{"text":" the actor’s placement","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"actors, room sets, candidates to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"roams"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"steals"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"reaction","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoMeleeCombat","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the combat ledger (health\/stun\/engagement by key)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"villains, weapons, prose to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"villain"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aggression"},{"type":"text","text":", and each villain’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"strikesFirst"},{"type":"text","text":" odds of picking a fight nobody offered him"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoSpellcasting","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the spell memory and the energy pool"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"spells + their ","type":"text"},{"code":"SpellCost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"spell(_:cost:effect:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoClock","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"the clock’s offset and pause state","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"start time, minutes per turn, alarms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"at(_:named:perform:)"},{"type":"text","text":", timetables to "},{"code":"schedule(_:daemonName:_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoConversation","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"the facts the player has worked out, and which answers each actor has already given","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"actors + topic rows to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"topics(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"again:"},{"type":"text","text":" lines for the answers that should land once), opening lines to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greeting(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", evidence to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shows(_:to:)"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The split follows one rule: a system that needs its own saved state is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bundle (its ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s namespace automatically and travel in","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"saves); a stateless toolkit is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GamePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Plugin prose arrives as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"init and factory parameters","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" with sensible defaults — ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fixed struct, so a plugin can’t add lines to it retroactively; what it can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"do is take its lines from the host, which also keeps every player-visible"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"string in the game’s own voice."}]},{"anchor":"Worked-examples","type":"heading","text":"Worked examples","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Lighthouse\/"},{"type":"text","text":" — a small host that splices just two: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoScoring"},{"type":"text","text":" (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"visit"},{"type":"text","text":" award and a one-off "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"awardOnce"},{"type":"text","text":", both declared in its award table so the bootstrap can check "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxScore"},{"text":") and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoActors"},{"text":" (a roaming keeper). The smallest of these examples.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Zork1\/Zork1.swift"},{"text":" — the host that wires four first-party plugins over entities from three content bundles.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Gramarye\/Gramarye.swift"},{"text":" — a small original game built entirely around ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoSpellcasting","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with one puzzle per casting paradigm.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Fulminate\/Fulminate.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" — the mystery demo, built around "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoClock"},{"type":"text","text":": an evening on a wall clock with three alarms bracketing it. Its story and mechanics contract live in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"docs\/games\/fulminate.md"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Sources\/KindlyDeep\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a survival-and-companion host: ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoActors.follows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a mule who trails you, is parked by a crawl he cannot fit through, and rejoins through a door, plus ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoScoring.awardOnce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on each of its five beats.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tests\/GnustoTests\/Support\/CommerceGame.swift"},{"text":" — the logic-only commerce plugin (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"buy"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sell"},{"text":" verbs, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"purchase"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sale"},{"text":" factories, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LampShop"},{"text":" host); ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PluginTests"},{"text":" drives a buy\/sell turn end to end.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Tests\/GnustoTests\/Support\/ShrineContent.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the content-bearing ","type":"text"},{"code":"ShrineContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin (owns a namespaced shrine region "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" exposes an "},{"code":"offering","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" factory) with its "},{"code":"PilgrimGame","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" host; "},{"code":"ContentPluginTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" drives a donate turn across the namespace boundary and checks the namespacing."}]}]}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/plugins"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Composing Large Games","anchor":"Composing-Large-Games","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/SplittingAGameAcros